{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>These are the generations of Aaron and Moses, etc.</b> And it enumerates only the generations of Aaron, to say that the sons of Aaron are counted for Moses, inasmuch as he prayed on their behalf and they lived, as it is written (Deuteronomy 9:20) ״ובאהרן התאנף ה׳ להשמידו״ etc., and they of blessed memory said (Leviticus Rabbah 7:1) that his prayer was effective to save Elazar and Itamar." "And the verse's saying <b>on the day that He spoke</b> etc., to tell the time when he prayed on their behalf. And it further includes in this the reason his prayer was accepted: it was because HaShem spoke to him on Mount Sinai, and he became a faithful emissary for HaShem in receiving the Torah."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:05:54.059848750Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}